.\" rl man page
.TH RL 1 "2026-09-24" "rl 2.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rl \- the rl programming language toolchain
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rl
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rl
is the command-line interface for the rl programming language. It provides
tools for running, checking, scaffolding, and packaging rl source files.
.PP
Standalone tools ship as separate binaries:
.BR rlc " (compiler), " rlt " (C transpiler), " rlrepl " (REPL), " rlsp " (LSP server), " rldocs " (docs viewer), and " rlm " (toolchain manager)."
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI run " FILE"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ \-\- " ARGS"]
Lex, parse, and evaluate a .rl source file. Arguments after the file path are
passed to the script as its argv.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BI \-c ", \-\-code " CODE
Execute inline rl code instead of a file.
.TP
.B \-\-vm
Run through the bytecode VM (highly experimental).
.RE
.TP
.B dev
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Run the current project by reading
.BR rl.toml .
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-vm
Run through the bytecode VM (highly experimental).
.RE
.TP
.BI new " NAME"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Scaffold a new project directory or create a standalone script.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Skip running
.B git init
in the new project.
.TP
.B \-\-script
Create a standalone .rl script instead of a project directory.
.TP
.B \-\-lib
Create a library project (generates src/lib.rl instead of src/main.rl).
.RE
.TP
.BI check " FILE"
Type-check a .rl file and report errors without running it.
.TP
.BI format " FILE"
Format a .rl source file in place.
.TP
.BI print " FILE"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Print debug information for a .rl source file. Exactly one of
.BR \-\-tokens ", " \-\-parser ", " "\-\-ast"
must be given.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BR \-t ", \-\-tokens"
Print the token stream.
.TP
.BR \-p ", \-\-parser"
Print the parsed AST (pre-type-check).
.TP
.BR \-a ", \-\-ast"
Print the type-checked AST.
.RE
.TP
.BI package " FILE"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
Package a .rl file into a self-contained binary.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BI \-o ", \-\-output " PATH
Output binary path. Defaults to "program".
.TP
.B \-\-vm
Compile to .rlc bytecode first and embed that (compressed) instead of the
raw source text.
.RE
.TP
.BI workflows " OPTIONS"
Scaffold GitHub Actions workflow files. At least one of
.B --check
or
.B --package
must be given.
.RS
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-check
Generate a workflow that runs
.B rl check
on push/PR.
.TP
.B \-\-package
Generate a workflow that packages and releases a binary.
.RE
.TP
.B pm
.I COMMAND
Manage project dependencies (downloads tarballs, verifies SHA256, links
into deps/). Commands:
.BR install ", " add ", " remove ", " list ", " update ", " cache "."
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RL_VERSION
Version to install for non-interactive install script use.
.TP
.B RL_INSTALL_DIR
Installation directory for the install script.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B rl.toml
Project configuration file read by
.BR "rl dev" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a script:
.RS
.PP
rl run hello.rl
.RE
.PP
Run with arguments:
.RS
.PP
rl run script.rl -- --verbose input.txt
.RE
.PP
Run inline code:
.RS
.PP
rl run -c 'println("hello")'
.RE
.PP
Start the REPL:
.RS
.PP
rlrepl
.RE
.PP
Type-check a file:
.RS
.PP
rl check script.rl
.RE
.PP
Create a new project:
.RS
.PP
rl new my_project
.RE
.PP
Transpile to C:
.RS
.PP
rlt script.rl --runtime --compile
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (type errors, I/O failures, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rlc (1),
.BR rlt (1)
